# What libgoldberry-media exports: the upstreams' own C APIs, one symbol a line,
# and the two functions of goldberry_media.c. Everything else in the library is
# local. Read by CMakeLists.txt, which forces each symbol out of its archive and
# lists it in the platform's export dialect; a line that is not a C identifier
# fails the configure step.
#
# The Java bindings under `dev.goldberry.media.ffm` name these and nothing
# else: a symbol a binding looks up and this list lacks fails at load, by name.

# --- goldberry_media.c -------------------------------------------------------
goldberry_media_abi
goldberry_media_versions

